-- title:
--   One-coordinate lift into the Fontaine kernel
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a commutative ring $\mathcal R$, a commutative ring $A$ and a surjective ring homomorphism $\pi\colon\mathcal R\to A$ whose kernel is contained in the ideal generated by $p$ in $\mathcal R$. Here, for $m:\mathbb N$, the subgroup `fontaineKer p m π` of the truncated Witt vectors $W_m(A)$ consists of those $a$ for which there is a Witt vector $X\in W(\mathcal R)$ with $\mathrm{truncate}_m(W(\pi)(X))=a$ and whose $(m-1)$-st ghost component lies in the ideal generated by $p^m$; and `frobeniusFun` is the coefficientwise $p$-th power map on $W_m(A)$, sending $x$ to the truncated Witt vector with coefficients $x_i^p$. Let $n:\mathbb N$ and let $u\in W_n(A)$ be such that the coefficientwise $p$-th power of $u$ lies in `fontaineKer p n π`. The assertion is that there exists $b\in W_{n+1}(A)$ lying in `fontaineKer p (n+1) π` whose truncation along $n\le n+1$ equals $u$; that is, $u$ extends by one further coordinate to a vector of length $n+1$ in the Fontaine kernel.
--
--   This is the elementary adjustment lemma used in the analysis of Fontaine's map $w$ attached to a surjection $\pi$ with kernel inside $p\mathcal R$: a covector whose coefficientwise $p$-th power lies in the kernel of $w$ can be completed by a last coordinate so as to land in the kernel of $w$ in the next length. It is invoked three times in the study of the Fontaine–Hodge filtration, by [`Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_add_eq_of_smul_eq_zero`](thm.html#Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_add_eq_of_smul_eq_zero), [`Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_frobenius_eq_smul`](thm.html#Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_frobenius_eq_smul) and [`Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_verschiebung_eq_of_frobenius_eq_zero`](thm.html#Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_verschiebung_eq_of_frobenius_eq_zero).
